From: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sudo: Include linux/types.h for __u64 in mount_attr fallback

The fallback definition of struct mount_attr, used when the C library
headers do not provide MOUNT_ATTR_SIZE_VER0, uses the kernel __u64 type.
With glibc >= 2.36 <sys/mount.h> includes <linux/mount.h>, so the
fallback is never compiled. musl's <sys/mount.h> does not, and none of
the other included headers pull in <linux/types.h>, so the build fails
with:

  sudo.cpp:111:5: error: unknown type name '__u64'

Include <linux/types.h> in the fallback block.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/src/systemui-lib/sudo/sudo.cpp
+++ b/src/systemui-lib/sudo/sudo.cpp
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@ extern "C" {
 #endif
 
 #ifndef MOUNT_ATTR_SIZE_VER0
+#  include <linux/types.h>
 #  define MOUNT_ATTR_SIZE_VER0 32
 struct mount_attr {
     __u64 attr_set;
